      </div>
      <div class="statcard statcard-purple">
        <div class="statcard-value">$26<span>B</span></div>
        <div class="statcard-label">Annual cost of employee theft to retailers (Appriss Retail)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="statcard statcard-blue">
        <div class="statcard-value">$2,180</div>
        <div class="statcard-label">Average loss per internal theft investigation (NRF)</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ IDENTITY ============ -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Identity &amp; Access</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Role-based permissions for every associate.</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Included with every deployment, no add-on required.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-row" style="margin-top: 16px;">
      <div class="feature-text">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Identity Management</span>
        <h2>Active Directory, SSO and MFA integration.</h2>
        <p>Centralized authentication, user roles, and device access across every application, running on the identity provider you already own.</p>
        <ul class="feature-bullets">
          <li>Integrates with Active Directory, SSO, and MFA, no separate user database to maintain</li>
          <li>Associate identities and permissions managed in one place, scoped per role</li>
          <li>Matrixed security rights across hundreds of individual corporate actions, not a handful of coarse presets</li>
          <li>Employee profile transfers tracked when someone moves between locations</li>
          <li>Device access governed alongside user access, tied to locations</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-visual">
        <div class="shot">
          <div class="shot-glow"></div>
          <img class="shot-img" src="/assets/images/homepage/tcs-svc-tap.webp" alt="Administration: a device record with users, roles, and privileges">
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-row reverse" style="margin-top: 56px;">
      <div class="feature-text">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Store Logins</span>
        <h2>Associate sign-in without shared passwords.</h2>
        <p>Secure, rotating QR-code logins for POS terminals and every application: shared credentials gone, every action attributable to a person.</p>
        <ul class="feature-bullets">
          <li>Rotating QR-code authentication that works even offline</li>
          <li>Username and password login enforcing character complexity and expiry timelines where you need it</li>
          <li>Every transaction tied to the individual who rang it</li>
          <li>Optional multi-user facial recognition on a shared device, identifying individual associates rather than a single enrolled iOS Face ID user</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="fine-note">Facial recognition is off by default and enabled at the retailer's discretion, with consent capture and retention periods configured by the retailer and subject to local biometric privacy law. QR-code and credential sign-in give you the same per-associate audit trail without processing biometric data.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-visual">
        <div class="shot">
          <div class="shot-glow"></div>
          <img class="shot-img shot-devices" src="/assets/images/homepage/teammate-card.webp" alt="Associate sign-in on iPhone, biometric authentication prompt">
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mini-grid mini-grid-2">
      <div class="mini-card">
        <div class="mini-ico"><i class="ti ti-devices"></i></div>
        <h3>Mobile device management</h3>
        <p>Register and manage company-owned and personal devices side by side, with application access and security policies controlled per device type.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mini-card">
        <div class="mini-ico"><i class="ti ti-users-group"></i></div>
        <h3>Team member management</h3>
        <p>Associate records, roles, and training assignments stay synchronized across every application, onboard once, and every tool knows who they are.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

